{"id": "EUVD-2026-82146", "enisaUuid": "96b495c2-5578-32ed-8310-258405bfdd55", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rxe: Validate num_sge/cur_sge before indexing wqe->dma.sge[]\n\nFor a user QP, qp->sq.queue is a ring the application writes directly,\nso rxe_post_send() takes the is_user branch and only schedules send_task\nwithout validating the WQE. rxe_requester() consumes it in place via\nreq_next_wqe() and calls copy_data(), which indexes\n&wqe->dma.sge[cur_sge] with the attacker-controlled num_sge/cur_sge.\nOnly the kernel path bounds num_sge (validate_send_wr()); the user WQE\nis never checked, so a local unprivileged user can post a WQE with an\nout-of-range cur_sge or oversized num_sge and force an out-of-bounds\nread of the per-WQE sge array in copy_data() (vmalloc OOB read, local\nDoS).\n\nBound num_sge to qp->sq.max_sge in rxe_requester() before use, the way\nget_srq_wqe() already guards SRQ entries, and bound cur_sge only when\nthe WQE carries payload (dma.resid): copy_data() returns early on a\nzero-length copy before touching dma->sge[], so a zero-payload WQE --\nthe only kind a max_sge == 0 QP can post -- stays valid.\n\nReproduced under KASAN; the vmalloc-out-of-bounds in copy_data() is gone.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69d3ccf6543f24c452a020c8028ca6f46cb1e8db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/750bba6ce9bb0b11d6a166031c9728ae3f21765e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c067aa7b231e91a18a1b3666201ab14dfb00347a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13cb7160e5b791f5e3ecf9311cf32849fe7e9b62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ec111ddc1f727c1e4580aea459842ae5a8359a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/126c757e4cd46f866ddc283143b58eb4d9bf52cd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92525", "GHSA-xqgc-mf52-qvg8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07cdec3e-68b2-3005-9faa-70e8386673ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "0de7bbe0-01b3-373d-b5d0-ed76b1f6e766", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "10846387-8934-31a6-8a8f-80fe8703f991", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "33e5642b-c000-3902-88a4-83bc2e78656a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <c067aa7b231e91a18a1b3666201ab14dfb00347a"}, {"id": "414b2929-0a09-3ca2-bfff-6a211dd3db9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "8b5cba7a-a3b5-3cc5-bedc-0cdd66e98ffa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <750bba6ce9bb0b11d6a166031c9728ae3f21765e"}, {"id": "8dd54c3f-8361-3708-b4b6-eca082b557c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <126c757e4cd46f866ddc283143b58eb4d9bf52cd"}, {"id": "900284aa-3ba0-32db-8104-b03ee102d7ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <5ec111ddc1f727c1e4580aea459842ae5a8359a5"}, {"id": "9255a73f-e609-3db9-a970-099b7ac86bea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8700e3e7c4857d28ebaa824509934556da0b3e76 <69d3ccf6543f24c452a020c8028ca6f46cb1e8db"}, {"id": "a2d32c0c-8969-3330-a3fb-6347244cb820", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "d6f2c1a6-5727-3af3-b85a-e79a8a87ffb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "e1c763eb-04df-33a0-9779-ae897f